  "verse.en:1KGS.17.1": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-10-27T21:01:17+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "First verse of the chapter, so there was no previous dramatic text to continue; the voice is set here. Glosses 21 and 22 correct STEPBible’s split “that / except”: kî ʾim is one unit, “except”. I kept the Masoretic mittôšābê as “resident aliens (dwellers)”. The BBE’s “of Tishbe in Gilead” follows another reading of the same consonants (from Tishbe); I recall the Septuagint reads it that way but did not verify. The Ugaritic points (Baal as Rider on the Clouds, dew as his daughter Ṭallay) are from my own background knowledge, not from the packet, so they have no source in the note. The Hiel / Joshua / Moses midrash is Rashi, Radak and Metzudat David and is labelled as rabbinic story, not text."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-10-27T21:19:40+00:00",
     "note": null
    }
   ]
  },
  "verse.en:1KGS.17.10": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-philologist@1",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-10-27T21:01:17+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "I contrast Rashi (Elijah does not recognise her, sets the Eliezer sign) with Malbim (he recognises her and probes). The Num 15:32–33 parallel for mĕqōšēš ʿēṣîm is from my own recall and hedged “as far as I can tell”. The “well-scene turned over” reading (Gen 24:17 has the same words, meʿaṭ-mayim) is mine."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-10-27T21:19:45+00:00",
     "note": null
    }
   ]
  },
  "verse.en:1KGS.17.11": {
